{number: 19}
{title: Take the Name of Jesus with You}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Take the name of Jesus with you,
[F] Child of sorrow [C] and of woe,
It will joy and comfort [G] give you,
[C] Take it, then, where-[G7] e’er you [C] go.
Precious [F] name, O how [C] sweet!
Hope of earth and joy of [G] heav’n;
Precious [C] name, [C7] O how [F] sweet!
[C] Hope of earth and [G7] joy of [C] heav’n.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Take the name of Jesus ever,
[F] As a shield from [C] every snare;
If temptations round you [G] gather,
[C] Breathe that holy [G7] name in [C] prayer.
Precious [F] name, O how [C] sweet!
Hope of earth and joy of [G] heav’n;
Precious [C] name, [C7] O how [F] sweet!
[C] Hope of earth and [G7] joy of [C] heav’n.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] O the precious name of Jesus!
[F] How it thrills our [C] souls with joy,
When His loving arms re-[G] ceive us,
[C] And His songs our [G7] tongues em-[C] ploy.
Precious [F] name, O how [C] sweet!
Hope of earth and joy of [G] heav’n;
Precious [C] name, [C7] O how [F] sweet!
[C] Hope of earth and [G7] joy of [C] heav’n.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[C] At the name of Jesus bowing,
[F] Falling prostrate [C] at His feet,
King of kings in heav’n we’ll [G] crown Him,
[C] When our journey [G7] is com-[C] plete.
Precious [F] name, O how [C] sweet!
Hope of earth and joy of [G] heav’n;
Precious [C] name, [C7] O how [F] sweet!
[C] Hope of earth and [G7] joy of [C] heav’n.
{end_of_verse}
